- op: discuss  # 9e00
  at: '2026-08-03T08:35:40Z'  # 9e00
  by: agent  # 9e00
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 9e00
  clock: 5  # 9e00
  nonce: '9e00'  # 9e00
  message: "DONE. Shipped in PR #184 (dev 1b7a1baee4) per the owner ruling: KEEP ORM reads as sources and make them SEPARABLE, rather than dropping or relabelling them.\n\nWHAT SHIPPED. AUTO_SOURCE_LABEL_MAP is many-to-one -- net_recv, ipc_recv and db_read all become the label untrusted_input -- and which boundary it was got discarded at the moment of derivation. TaintSource and TaintFlowFinding now carry source_boundary; each taint verdict carries a flow_origins breakdown keyed by it; each evidence row carries it for drill-down. Envelope schema 1.2 -> 1.3. Spec updated.\n\nNO NEW VOCABULARY WAS MINTED. The distinction already existed as io_boundary's controlled categories and was simply being thrown away, so this carries the existing axis through rather than promoting a new db_at_rest / external one. That is the ADR-0024 / R1 new-axis reversal (\"the fact already has a home -- consolidate ONTO it\") rather than a new typed field. `declared` buckets YAML-declared sources, which have no boundary.\n\nBEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE (9-repo cohort, cohort-vazal vs cohort-bifob; instrument asserted in BOTH directions first, and the pre-fix tree could not run the new signature at all):\n  verdict changes    0        (38 confirmed / 16 violated, identical both arms)\n  evidence rows      270 -> 270, unchanged\n  flow_origins       db_read 186 · env_read 111 · net_recv 14\nThe zero is the POINT, not a disappointing result: the ruling was to keep the flows and make them legible, so any verdict movement would have meant the change had become the relabelling option the owner declined. The instrument asserts non-destructiveness explicitly, because a run where db_read flows quietly stopped matching would produce a CLEANER-LOOKING number while silently measuring the wrong option.\n\nWHAT IT BUYS, per violated claim:\n  pretix/untrusted-input-no-database    {db_read: 140}          entirely ORM churn\n  pretix/untrusted-input-no-host-fs     {db_read: 31}\n  pretix/untrusted-input-no-subprocess  {db_read: 13}\n  kserve/untrusted-input-no-host-fs     {db_read: 2, net_recv: 5}  mostly REAL external input\n  caddy/untrusted-input-no-network      {net_recv: 1}\n  alertmanager/host-secret-no-logging   {env_read: 57}\nA reader can now tell pretix's database claim is ORM noise while kserve's filesystem claim is genuine network input. Both wore the identical label before, so that distinction was structurally unavailable.\n\nTWO OF MY OWN EARLIER CLAIMS ON THIS ITEM ARE HEREBY CORRECTED, and the feature is what caught them.\n  (1) \"Dropping ORM reads changes ZERO verdicts\" -- the measurement that de-ranked this item against WI-kabif section 3a. WRONG.\n  (2) The later \"correction\" that 7 non-ORM flows remained on pretix/untrusted-input-no-database, so ORM was not holding it. ALSO WRONG, and wrong in the opposite direction.\nBoth came from a hand-rolled ORM predicate whose read-set was {filter, get, all, values, values_list, first, last, exists, count} and therefore MISSED exclude, none, annotate and select_related -- all genuine Django reads. Production classifies 100 of 100 shown rows as db_read where my predicate found 93.\nTHE CORRECTED NUMBER: dropping db_read-sourced flows would flip 3 of 16 violated claims to confirmed -- pretix/untrusted-input-no-database (140), -no-host-fs (31), -no-subprocess (13). So the relabelling option the owner DECLINED would have silently changed three verdicts, which makes that ruling better-founded than the evidence available when it was made. The item's value is also higher than the \"output readability only\" framing I gave: this class is load-bearing for three claims, not merely noise.\nROOT CAUSE, three times in one session (a test-vs-production path regex, a .text/.message accessor, this read-set): I counted with a predicate I wrote instead of the one production runs. L53. The rule worth carrying: when a production classification exists for the thing you are counting, counting it yourself IS the bug.\n\nRESIDUAL, disclosed rather than implied: 40 of pretix/untrusted-input-no-database's 140 flows are above the _MAX_EVIDENCE_ROWS cap and so are not individually displayed. flow_origins counts FLOWS (140) rather than displayed rows (100), so the breakdown is complete even where the row list is truncated -- but no per-row claim about those 40 is supported."  # 9e00
